# The edge catalogue's known failures, and the ticket that owns each.
#
# One per line: `<story>::<arm>`, a tab, and the ticket. `story_edges.rs` reads
# it when a case answers something other than what the pinned SQLite answers.
#
# **An entry that no longer describes a failure is itself a failure**, so when
# the ticket lands the story goes red until the line is removed. That is the
# rule from task-1969 section 4: a list that only grows is a list of things
# nobody will take off it, and a fixed defect left listed reads as coverage and
# is not.
a_dropped_and_recreated_table_rolls_back::default	task-2043: a rolled back DROP then CREATE of the same table loses every row, durably
a_dropped_and_recreated_table_rolls_back::sqlite_page	task-2043: a rolled back DROP then CREATE of the same table loses every row, durably
a_dropped_and_recreated_table_rolls_back::small_pool	task-2043: a rolled back DROP then CREATE of the same table loses every row, durably
a_dropped_and_recreated_table_rolls_back::truncate_journal	task-2043: a rolled back DROP then CREATE of the same table loses every row, durably
a_dropped_and_recreated_table_rolls_back::persist_journal	task-2043: a rolled back DROP then CREATE of the same table loses every row, durably
a_dropped_and_recreated_table_rolls_back::waiting	task-2043: a rolled back DROP then CREATE of the same table loses every row, durably
